A_647 - Personally I have some doubt about whether sugar is really what causes cavities: saliva helps digest sugars, among other things, so I wonder if the link is as direct as commonly claimed. I've also personally found that, over more than 15 consecutive years without brushing my teeth while following a meat-free diet, I haven't had any cavities, and I made a TikTok video about this too. I do want to make clear, though, that this is my own personal, isolated experience, not advice to follow: the scientific community and dentists consistently recommend daily oral hygiene for everyone, regardless of diet, and it's best to stick to that guidance.